    /* ── Read & Learn ── */
    'lire.hero.breadcrumb':   'Financial education',
    'lire.hero.tag':          'Reading · Learning · Financial education',
    'lire.hero.title':        'Read, learn and<br><em>manage your money better</em>',
    'lire.meta.readTime':     ' 6 min read',
    'lire.meta.tags':         'Education · Books · Resources',
    'lire.lead':              '"There\'s a difference between knowing something and truly applying it in your life. Sometimes, hearing the right idea at the right moment is enough to change everything."',
    'lire.p1':                'I must admit that the advice I share can sometimes seem simple — even obvious to some people. These aren\'t revolutionary strategies or ultra-complex concepts. But over time, I\'ve understood that there\'s a big difference between <strong>knowing something</strong> and actually applying it day to day.',
    'lire.p2':                'Sometimes, an idea heard at the right moment simply acts as a reminder. A reminder of notions we already knew, but had set aside. And that\'s often how real changes begin — with a small moment of awareness.',
    'lire.h2.why':            'Why financial education matters so much',
    'lire.p3':                'The problem with finances is that when you don\'t understand a money-related topic, you tend to avoid it completely. You tell yourself it\'s too complicated, that you don\'t have the necessary knowledge, that you\'ll look into it later.',
    'lire.p4':                'But years go by fast. And financial mistakes accumulate: bad habits, no savings, debt, fear of investing, poor tax management. At some point, you have to accept talking about it — and getting serious about it.',
    'lire.pullquote':         '"All the knowledge I\'ve acquired, I developed on my own. I\'m neither a financial planner nor an advisor. I\'m simply someone who loves to learn."',
    'lire.h2.how':            'How I learn — my main sources',
    'lire.res1.title':        'Personal finance books',
    'lire.res1.desc':         'The psychology of money, financial habits, long-term investing — I\'ve always genuinely loved reading, and books remain my favorite source of learning.',
    'lire.res2.title':        'Podcasts while working',
    'lire.res2.desc':         'I listen to podcasts on finance, investing and tax while I work in my business. By regularly consuming educational content, the concepts naturally integrate over time.',
    'lire.res3.title':        'Online courses',
    'lire.res3.desc':         'Revenu Québec offers free training for self-employed workers. Cégep Beauce-Appalaches offers tax training for entrepreneurs. Accessible resources that prevent many costly mistakes.',
    'lire.res4.title':        'Blogs and honest accounts',
    'lire.res4.desc':         'Reading accounts from people who speak honestly about their relationship with money — their mistakes, their successes, their reflections. Money remains a very sensitive topic in our society, and talking about it in a healthy way really helps.',
    'lire.h2.livres':         'My recommended books',
    'lire.p5':                'You\'ll see several book recommendations on this site. These are works that personally helped me change the way I think about money.',
    'lire.livre1.why':        '→ Rethinking the balance between living today and preparing for tomorrow',
    'lire.livre2.why':        '→ Understanding your emotional relationship with money',
    'lire.livre3.title':      'The Richest Man in Babylon',
    'lire.livre3.why':        '→ The timeless basics of saving and investing',
    'lire.livre4.why':        '→ Investing simply with long-term ETFs',
    'lire.livre5.why':        '→ Automating your finances and stopping the guilt',
    'lire.livre6.why':        '→ How real millionaires think and live',
    'lire.h2.ressources':     'Free resources in Quebec',
    'lire.formations.title':  'Going further — for free',
    'lire.form1.span':        'Bookkeeping, tax management for self-employed workers. Essential to avoid costly mistakes.',
    'lire.form2.span':        'lautorite.qc.ca — Free guides on TFSA, RRSP, investing, retirement. The Quebec reference.',
    'lire.form3.span':        'Tax training for entrepreneurs. Knowledge that can save thousands of dollars.',
    'lire.form4.span':        'French-language content, Quebec-specific. TFSA, RRSP, ETFs, retirement explained simply.',
    'lire.form5.span':        'Quebec blog on retirement, investing and financial freedom. Very accessible.',
    'lire.highlight':         'I\'m starting a tax training program myself soon. Once completed, <strong>I\'ll write an article to share what I\'ve learned</strong> and how I plan to apply it in my own reality. Stay tuned.',
    'lire.h2.reinvest':       'The money I save, I reinvest',
    'lire.p6':                'For people who aren\'t comfortable managing their finances alone, there are competent financial planners. Personally, it\'s not an avenue I use for now — simply because I love learning, understanding and managing on my own.',
    'lire.p7':                'And honestly? <strong>Every dollar saved in fees or bad decisions, I prefer to reinvest.</strong> Because ultimately, every dollar saved today can become an asset that keeps growing through compound interest.',
    'lire.p8':                'You don\'t retain everything you read. But sometimes, a single idea is enough to change a habit — and small repeated changes over many years can have an enormous impact on a person\'s financial stability.',
    'lire.disclaimer':        ' I am not a financial advisor. This article shares my personal experience and favorite resources — not official financial advice.',
    'lire.sidebar.title':     'Start investing',
    'lire.sidebar.body':      'Wealthsimple — the platform I use. Free, no commission.',
